            "review_title": "Review at Pho Ngoc",
            "review_text": "Tess W\nBrisbane, Australia32 contributions\n1\nAmazing Pho in Ho Chi Minh - a must try\nJun 2017 • Family\nWe visited this Pho street cafe after seeing it on a TV show \"Luke Nguyen's Street Food Asia\" and we experienced the most amazing Pho and friendly service. The owner is a lovely Vietnamese lady who has been making and serving her family recipe of Pho for over 30 years. She sets up her cafe in a little laneway in front of her house, opened from 05:00 - 10:30am every day. We have had Pho many times in Australia and a couple of times in Vietnam previously. On this visit to Vietnam, we thought we'd give this place a try. We were certainly not disappointed - it was so much better than any we have had before. What made it even better is that it was in a little local family cafe, which we love to support when we travel. \nCost in total for 3 of us was $12 AUD and that included a milk iced coffee as well as a large Pho each. We tried to leave a tip but the owner wouldn't accept it. \nWe caught an Uber to Pho Ngoc and they had no problem finding the place. Cost for an Uber to there from our hotel was less than $2 AUD. \nIf you are wanting some amazing local Pho then this place is a must.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten June 30, 2017",
